<article class="env-lemma" id="0CMF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CMF">Lemma <span data-tag="0CMF">70.22.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ and $h : U \to X$ be morphisms of algebraic spaces over $S$. Assume that $Y$ is locally Noetherian, that $f$ and $h$ are of finite type, that $f$ is quasi-separated, and that $h(U)$ is dense in $X$. If given any commutative solid diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(K) \ar[r] \ar[d] &  U \ar[r]^ h &  X \ar[d]^ f \\  \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A) \ar[rr] \ar@{-->}[rru] &  &  Y }  \]
</div>
  <p> where $A$ is a discrete valuation ring with field of fractions $K$, there exists a unique dotted arrow making the diagram commute, then $f$ is proper. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Lemmas <a href="/tag/0CME" data-tag="0CME">70.22.2</a> and <a href="/tag/0CMD" data-tag="0CMD">70.22.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>